Subject: [PATCH] BT LOCKDOWN v2 mobile contract: /sync endpoint, UTC Z times,
 real stats, logout, rate limit, device expiry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- teaching_mobile.py:
  * GET /api/lockdown/sync — one round-trip for the phone's 4s poll
    (current session + timetable + user with real stats).
  * All server times now explicit UTC ISO-8601 with Z suffix (phone
    parses naive as UTC too). Fixes phantom 2-hour clock-drift
    penalties for devices outside UTC.
  * /me returns real sessionsCompleted/minutesLocked and the bound
    device; applies pending penalties so ELO is fresh immediately.
  * POST /api/lockdown/logout unbinds the device.
  * Login rate limit (8/15min per id+ip -> 429 too_many_attempts).
  * Device binding idle 14+ days -> 401 device_expired (login route
    stays open for re-pairing); heartbeat refreshed opportunistically.
- app.py /api/lockdown/current: server_time and end_time now Z-suffixed
  UTC (fallback endpoint for phones on the new build).
